♪ I'm gonna show you what I'm made of ♪

457
00:20:59,424 --> 00:21:03,470
♪ How do you like me now?
Whoa whoa ♪

458
00:21:04,179 --> 00:21:07,057
♪ I'm gonna show you I was born for this ♪

459
00:21:07,140 --> 00:21:11,186
♪ How do you like me now?
Whoa whoa… ♪

460
00:21:12,354 --> 00:21:14,856
-Man, this looks good.
-Oh, man.

461
00:21:15,315 --> 00:21:17,109
[Jason] This place looks awesome.

462
00:21:17,192 --> 00:21:20,821
-[Brett] How many people was it, 40?
-[Jason] Damn. It's like torture,

463
00:21:20,904 --> 00:21:21,989
walking around here.

464
00:21:22,864 --> 00:21:24,866
We've been doing Friendsgiving
at the Oppenheim Group

465
00:21:24,950 --> 00:21:26,493
for, I think, five years now.

466
00:21:26,576 --> 00:21:29,830
This night is the confluence
of all of my favorite things.

467
00:21:29,913 --> 00:21:32,582
It's all my family
and all my closest friends.

468
00:21:32,666 --> 00:21:35,836
The food is epic.
It's, like, my favorite meal of the year

469
00:21:35,919 --> 00:21:38,255
and my favorite night of the year,
all in one.

470
00:21:38,338 --> 00:21:41,341
We're lucky, man.
Great friends, great family.

471
00:21:41,425 --> 00:21:42,426
Yeah.

472
00:21:42,509 --> 00:21:43,969
-It's gonna be fun.
-It's a cool day. 

473
00:21:44,052 --> 00:21:46,304
I like it right now when it's just us,
no one's here.

474
00:21:46,388 --> 00:21:47,347
[laughs] All this food.

475
00:21:48,682 --> 00:21:50,892
-[Romain] The food is ready?
-[Mary laughs] Hey!

476
00:21:50,976 --> 00:21:53,061
-How pretty.
-[Jason] I did it myself. Come on in.

477
00:21:53,478 --> 00:21:54,938
Hey, babe. Thanks for making it.

478
00:21:55,022 --> 00:21:57,399
-Wow. It's so big.
-So pretty.

479
00:21:57,482 --> 00:21:59,860
-[Jason] Happy Thanksgiving, beautiful.
-Happy Thanksgiving.

480
00:21:59,943 --> 00:22:01,153
[Mary] Are you eating already?

481
00:22:01,236 --> 00:22:02,571
-[Romain] No.
-You look nice, Ma.

482
00:22:02,654 --> 00:22:05,657
-Thank you.
-[Jason] Mama. Oh, good to see you.

483
00:22:05,741 --> 00:22:07,034
JT in the house.

484
00:22:07,117 --> 00:22:08,869
-Hi, guys.
-Damn, girl. How are you?

485
00:22:08,952 --> 00:22:11,121
[Romain] Aïe, aïe, aïe,
you gonna be in trouble.

486
00:22:11,204 --> 00:22:13,331
-[Chrishell] Should we sit?
-[Maya] Are we sitting down?

487
00:22:13,832 --> 00:22:19,254
[screams] Oh, my God!
Boob almost fell out. [giggles]

488
00:22:19,338 --> 00:22:22,174
[Jason] Chrishell,
your dream has come true with that bell.

489
00:22:22,257 --> 00:22:23,550
You are the inspiration.

490
00:22:23,633 --> 00:22:27,512
We need a bell. Every time someone
closes something, we, like, ring the bell.

491
00:22:27,679 --> 00:22:29,264
[Chrishell] I am so excited.

492
00:22:29,348 --> 00:22:32,059
-I can't wait to, like…
-[Jason] You're the official bell ringer.

493
00:22:32,142 --> 00:22:33,727
One hit per million.

494
00:22:33,810 --> 00:22:35,145
Jason, that's giant.

495
00:22:35,228 --> 00:22:38,273
-If I had a nickel…
-Oh, my God.

496
00:22:38,940 --> 00:22:40,776
-All right, everyone…
-[glasses clinking]

497
00:22:40,859 --> 00:22:42,152
…dinner time!

498
00:22:42,235 --> 00:22:43,904
[Mary laughs] Don't have to tell me twice.

499
00:22:43,987 --> 00:22:45,447
-Let's do it.
-[Brett] Go ahead.

500
00:22:45,530 --> 00:22:48,200
-I should've brought a vegan pumpkin pie.
-[Brett] I'm gonna taste it.

501
00:22:48,283 --> 00:22:51,495
-[Chrishell] You feeling brave?
-[Jason] Do a little bit more dark meat.

502
00:22:51,578 --> 00:22:54,122
-[Mary] What's this thing?
-[Chrishell] It's macaroni that's sweet.

503
00:22:54,206 --> 00:22:55,874
[Heather] I don't know if I can have this.

504
00:22:55,957 --> 00:22:58,543
[Chrishell] I thought there was just
one station. I didn't know

505
00:22:58,627 --> 00:23:01,088
-it was gonna keep going like this.
-[Heather] I'll get veggies.

506
00:23:01,171 --> 00:23:03,423
-[Maya] Mashed potatoes, nice.
-[Jason] Best thing here.

507
00:23:03,507 --> 00:23:05,967
-[Mary] What is it?
-[Heather] Is there butter? I don't know

508
00:23:06,051 --> 00:23:08,470
-if there is.
-[Jason] Very high class, so it's good.

509
00:23:11,640 --> 00:23:14,309
I can't believe I'm drinking
Oppenheim Group wine. Jesus Christ.

510
00:23:14,726 --> 00:23:15,560
Seconds, Pops?

511
00:23:16,561 --> 00:23:18,480
[Christine] That's how you know
I was desperate.

512
00:23:18,563 --> 00:23:21,650
-It's not good. I don't like it at all.
-It's not, it's awful.

513
00:23:22,192 --> 00:23:25,404
I'm actually excited to leave
on a holiday. I usually always just do

514
00:23:25,487 --> 00:23:27,280
something with family,
so it's fun to get away.

515
00:23:27,364 --> 00:23:30,408
-[Chrishell] Where are you guys going?
-We're doing Amsterdam first, then Paris.

516
00:23:30,492 --> 00:23:32,119
-[Chrishell] For Thanksgiving?
-Mm-hmm.

517
00:23:32,202 --> 00:23:35,789
Are you expecting anything special
to happen in Paris?

518
00:23:35,872 --> 00:23:37,499
It's always risky to take a girl to Paris,

519
00:23:37,582 --> 00:23:39,918
because they're always
gonna be expecting something.

520
00:23:42,003 --> 00:23:45,507
I don't know. I feel, like, I don't wanna
go into it with expectations.

521
00:23:45,590 --> 00:23:48,677
Of course, I'd say yes,
and I can't wait to marry him, but…

522
00:23:48,760 --> 00:23:50,512
um, I can wait as well.

523
00:23:51,263 --> 00:23:53,014
I have a feeling.

524
00:23:53,515 --> 00:23:56,852
Well, we are having dinner
with his jeweler later tonight, so…

525
00:23:56,935 --> 00:23:59,312
-[Chrishell] Are you serious? Oh, my Gosh!
-[Jason] No way.

526
00:23:59,396 --> 00:24:01,857
-And we did try on rings, so…
-[Jason] Oh, wow.

527
00:24:01,940 --> 00:24:04,693
[Mary] Yeah, it's happening. [laughs]
-Can you send us a group text

528
00:24:04,776 --> 00:24:06,820
if it happens?
-[Maya] We don't wanna find out

529
00:24:06,903 --> 00:24:08,113
-on Instagram.
-No.

530
00:24:08,196 --> 00:24:09,614
Hey, guys. Where's Amanza?

531
00:24:09,698 --> 00:24:12,701
You're doing the project with her.
Does she even show up at all?

532
00:24:12,784 --> 00:24:14,870
-Like, she helps?
-[Heather] It's a lot of stress on me

533
00:24:14,953 --> 00:24:17,164
'cause Amanza is staging,
but she couldn't show up.

534
00:24:17,247 --> 00:24:20,167
-So I had to go pick art for the house.
-You went to the gallery?

535
00:24:20,250 --> 00:24:23,253
-[Heather] She's doing personal stuff.
-Aren't we all, though?

536
00:24:23,336 --> 00:24:24,337
[laughter]

537
00:24:24,421 --> 00:24:27,591
I mean, I have a good eye, I think.
I just hope it looks good with the-- 

538
00:24:27,674 --> 00:24:29,384
I don't know
how the furniture's gonna look.

539
00:24:29,467 --> 00:24:30,886
[Maya] I call her Messy Nancy.

540
00:24:30,969 --> 00:24:32,846
-I know.
-It's always something.

541
00:24:32,929 --> 00:24:35,599
-[Christine, Maya] She's late, sick…
-[Maya] Then she doesn't show up,

542
00:24:35,682 --> 00:24:37,392
-she forgot her phone in an Uber.
-I know.

543
00:24:37,476 --> 00:24:40,687
She break into an open house.
There is always, like, an event.

544
00:24:41,104 --> 00:24:43,648
This whole situation
with Amanza and her kids

545
00:24:43,732 --> 00:24:45,859
is just really taking a toll on her.

546
00:24:45,942 --> 00:24:48,653
It's heartbreaking to watch Amanza 

547
00:24:48,737 --> 00:24:51,781
and those two beautiful kids
go through all of this.

548
00:24:51,865 --> 00:24:53,575
I think it's very important

549
00:24:53,658 --> 00:24:57,495
that she spends this quality time
on Thanksgiving with her kids.

550
00:24:57,579 --> 00:25:00,916
And that's something
that she needs to tell everybody.

551
00:25:00,999 --> 00:25:02,292
It's not my place.

552
00:25:03,585 --> 00:25:05,045
[Heather] So excited for the wedding.

553
00:25:05,128 --> 00:25:06,963
Oh, my God,
our cake is gonna be really pretty.

554
00:25:07,047 --> 00:25:08,173
I can't wait till you see it.

555
00:25:08,256 --> 00:25:09,716
[Jason clinks a glass] Guys.

556
00:25:10,675 --> 00:25:11,676
Quick toast.

557
00:25:12,093 --> 00:25:14,930
Listen, everybody,
this is my favorite evening of the year.

558
00:25:15,013 --> 00:25:16,556
All my friends and family,

559
00:25:16,932 --> 00:25:18,516
all my cousins, aunts, uncles,

560
00:25:18,600 --> 00:25:20,185
my best friends and co-workers.

561
00:25:20,268 --> 00:25:22,562
So much to be thankful for
on this Thanksgiving,

562
00:25:22,646 --> 00:25:23,897
so I couldn't be happier.

563
00:25:24,022 --> 00:25:28,193
I love all of you, and I just wanna toast
to how fortunate we all are.

564
00:25:28,944 --> 00:25:31,154
-[Heather] Cheers to that.
-[all] Cheers, everyone.

565
00:25:32,030 --> 00:25:34,491
Sorry, and there's one more thing
that I'm thankful for.

566
00:25:34,574 --> 00:25:36,576
I just closed
on a 44 million dollar house.

567
00:25:36,660 --> 00:25:38,453
[all] What?
[screaming, applause]

568
00:25:39,454 --> 00:25:40,288
Cheers!

569
00:25:40,914 --> 00:25:42,874
[Mary] Oh, my God!

570
00:25:43,083 --> 00:25:45,669
[Jason] The biggest sale
in the history of the Oppenheim Group.

571
00:25:45,752 --> 00:25:47,462
[Mary repeating] I had a feeling.

572
00:25:47,796 --> 00:25:49,047
Oh, my God!

573
00:25:49,464 --> 00:25:54,803
I wish it was me. I mean, it would be nice
to sell a 43 million dollar listing.

574
00:25:54,886 --> 00:25:57,180
Would be a nice commission.
But you know what?

575
00:25:57,931 --> 00:26:00,100
Jason worked hard, and he deserve it,

576
00:26:00,183 --> 00:26:03,270
so I'm not going to hate,
I'm going to congratulate.

577
00:26:03,687 --> 00:26:05,522
So congratulations, Jason.

578
00:26:05,939 --> 00:26:06,898
Mazel tov!

579
00:26:07,315 --> 00:26:09,276
-Chrishell, would you go ring the bell?
-Oh, can I?

580
00:26:09,359 --> 00:26:10,360
Yeah.

581
00:26:10,443 --> 00:26:11,903
[cheering, applause]

582
00:26:13,530 --> 00:26:18,243
-[bell clanging loudly]
-[wild cheering]

583
00:26:18,326 --> 00:26:20,245
[Heather] Yes, your dream come true!

584
00:26:20,328 --> 00:26:23,206
-[Chrishell] That's so exciting!
-I know, thank you, guys.

585
00:26:23,290 --> 00:26:25,333
You kept this a secret from us?

586
00:26:25,417 --> 00:26:27,419
-Who is the buyer, Jason?
-I can't say.

587
00:26:27,502 --> 00:26:29,254
I signed an NDA,
so I can't really say much.

588
00:26:29,337 --> 00:26:31,339
Remember when we were talking?
I was giving you shit?

589
00:26:31,423 --> 00:26:33,383
Remember, I had a showing
the next morning?

590
00:26:33,466 --> 00:26:34,426
Yeah? Oh, that one!

591
00:26:34,509 --> 00:26:37,679
-Jason, I'm so happy for you.
-[Jason] Thank you, guys. Me too.

592
00:26:37,762 --> 00:26:41,182
-[Chrishell] Let's have dessert.
-[Brett] Come on, dessert. Let's go!

593
00:26:45,061 --> 00:26:46,771
Boom. I waited all year for this.

594
00:26:46,855 --> 00:26:48,106
[laughs]

595
00:26:48,189 --> 00:26:49,441
-Jason.
-[Jason] Hey.

596
00:26:49,524 --> 00:26:52,360
-I just wanna say congratulations.
-Oh, thank you, honey.

597
00:26:53,194 --> 00:26:55,071
Sorry I gave you a hard time
the other day.

598
00:26:55,155 --> 00:26:56,031
Oh, come on.

599
00:26:56,114 --> 00:26:58,283
That's amazing
that you put that in escrow.

600
00:26:58,450 --> 00:27:00,994
I am really excited for Jason
that he sold Hillside.

601
00:27:01,077 --> 00:27:05,123
I know how hard it is 'cause I was, like,
trying to sell my expensive listing.

602
00:27:05,206 --> 00:27:08,543
No, you don't have to ever apologize.
I feel like I'm too tough on you.

603
00:27:08,627 --> 00:27:10,086
That's sweet. Thank you.

604
00:27:10,837 --> 00:27:14,299
The reason I'm so tough on you is
'cause, honestly, you have more potential

605
00:27:14,382 --> 00:27:16,259
-than anyone I can think of.
-I appreciate that.

606
00:27:16,343 --> 00:27:19,804
I just value your time tremendously,
and I think that you should, too.

607
00:27:20,221 --> 00:27:21,973
Absolutely, I agree with you. [laughs]

608
00:27:22,057 --> 00:27:25,226
[Jason] Honestly, if I wasn't hard on you,
that's when you should be concerned.

609
00:27:25,310 --> 00:27:27,646
I'm only hard on people
that I really believe in.

610
00:27:27,729 --> 00:27:31,024
'Cause it takes energy
to be engaged and to care.

611
00:27:31,274 --> 00:27:33,526
-A hundred percent. Yeah.
-So, if I'm never upset,

612
00:27:33,610 --> 00:27:35,862
then you're doing something wrong.

613
00:27:35,945 --> 00:27:36,946
Good.

614
00:27:37,030 --> 00:27:39,449
Oh, my God, I do want dessert.
Let's get dessert.

615
00:27:40,033 --> 00:27:43,328
-Oh, my God. That bourbon-pecan--
-That blueberry pie is--

616
00:27:43,411 --> 00:27:45,413
-Mary.
-Yeah?

617
00:27:45,497 --> 00:27:47,999
You did a great job on Doheny.
I'm gonna bring you on Alpine.

618
00:27:48,083 --> 00:27:49,668
[Mary] Oh, my God.

619
00:27:49,751 --> 00:27:51,795
-That is awesome! 
-That's exciting.

620
00:27:52,170 --> 00:27:54,756
I have a client in Beverly Hills
who is looking to sell his property

621
00:27:54,839 --> 00:27:55,965
for about 9.5.

622
00:27:56,591 --> 00:27:58,760
-[Jason] You ready for that?
-Thank you! Yes, I'm ready.

623
00:27:58,843 --> 00:28:01,262
-[Jason] Gonna rely on you, so…
-I'm all yours.

624
00:28:01,346 --> 00:28:03,139
-Easy.
-[Jason, Mary laugh]

625
00:28:03,223 --> 00:28:04,099
Can't be stopped.

626
00:28:04,808 --> 00:28:06,142
[Maya] Are you kidding me?

627
00:28:06,226 --> 00:28:09,396
I get it. We cannot expect Jason
to give all of us deals.

628
00:28:09,479 --> 00:28:13,566
I'm just saying, maybe share a little bit
because we all work hard, and…

629
00:28:13,650 --> 00:28:17,070
I just feel like,
at times, it's a little bit unfair.

630
00:28:17,487 --> 00:28:20,073
In this business, you always have
to hustle no matter what, right?

631
00:28:20,156 --> 00:28:21,658
Because nobody giving you anything.

632
00:28:21,741 --> 00:28:26,871
It's just hurting a little bit
to see that someone gets more than us.

633
00:28:26,955 --> 00:28:29,082
'Cause, you know that with Jason and Mary,

634
00:28:29,165 --> 00:28:31,334
like, of course she's closing,
of course she does things,

635
00:28:31,418 --> 00:28:34,212
because he gives her buyers,
listings, so it's easy.

636
00:28:34,295 --> 00:28:37,716
Jason and I have been friends
for probably 15 years.

637
00:28:38,341 --> 00:28:41,469
We dated for maybe a year of that.

638
00:28:41,928 --> 00:28:44,764
These girls are trying
to take away all of my success

639
00:28:44,848 --> 00:28:47,726
and my hard work, saying,
"Oh, it's 'cause they dated."

640
00:28:47,809 --> 00:28:48,643
No!

641
00:28:49,018 --> 00:28:51,646
I bust my ass, and I've worked for it.

642
00:28:51,730 --> 00:28:54,315
And I think it's extremely rude
and disrespectful

643
00:28:54,399 --> 00:28:57,235
to try to take my accomplishments and my--

644
00:28:57,318 --> 00:29:00,697
all of my hard work away from me
because I'm a successful woman,

645
00:29:00,780 --> 00:29:03,533
and they wanna throw it back on,
"She's probably sleeping with him."

646
00:29:03,616 --> 00:29:04,451
No!

647
00:29:05,243 --> 00:29:09,205
But what about the rest?
We all work hard, we all do open houses.

648
00:29:09,289 --> 00:29:11,875
Like, when are we gonna be good enough,
you know?

649
00:29:16,671 --> 00:29:18,214
["Not Worth It" playing]

650
00:29:20,216 --> 00:29:23,845
♪ Fool me once, fool me twice
On purpose ♪

651
00:29:23,928 --> 00:29:29,517
♪ I don't play all your games
You lie-ie-ie ♪

652
00:29:29,601 --> 00:29:31,603
♪ You're not worth it… ♪

